course: dictionary
lesson: 3114
title: Elected: chosen by a vote
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When people vote, they choose who will do a job. Elected means chosen this way. A class representative who gets the most votes is elected.
explain: «Separation of powers means splitting power between the lawmakers, the government and the courts, so no one part gets too strong; some people say unelected judges should not overrule elected leaders.» Elected leaders are the people the public voted for. Unelected judges are the ones nobody voted for. The prefix un- means not, so unelected means not chosen by a vote.
explain: Elected can also describe a person, as in an elected leader. It can also be followed by to, as in «They elected to stay late», which means they chose to do it. Look for clue words like voted, chosen and votes.
fact: Elected means chosen by people voting.
fact: As an adjective, elected describes a person who got their job by a vote, like an elected leader.
fact: Class representatives, school councils and mayors are often elected.
fact: Useful phrases: elected by, elected as, newly elected, democratically elected, elected to.
fact: The opposite of elected in the sentence is unelected, which means not chosen by a vote.
exercise: The class voted, and Mia was elected class representative. What does elected mean? | Sent to the head teacher | *Chosen by people voting | Moved to a new class | Given a prize for good work
exercise: «Some people say unelected judges should not overrule elected leaders.» What does unelected mean? | Very loud | *Not chosen by a vote | Chosen by a vote | Very old
exercise: In the phrase «the newly elected school council», what does newly tell you? | *It was chosen by a vote recently | It is a brand new building | It has no members at all | It was chosen by a teacher alone
test: Jamal elected to stay after school to help. What does elected to mean here? | Was sent home early | Was given a ticket | Was voted out of the club | *Chose to do something
test: Which phrase shows a leader got the job by people voting? | barely awake | very tall | ancient castle | *democratically elected
exam: The pupils ____ their school council every year by voting. Which word fits best? | famished | *elected | glum | curt
